# Stage 1 of Myth (TZX block 40 at $6C3F-$F03E): the annotations kit/mkgame.py writes src/stage1/*.asm from.
#
# The case's main part (case.json). Stages 2-5 (src/stage2..5) are the same engine assembled at other addresses;
# tools/stage_names.py carries this file's names over to them. The resident part $F03F-$FFFF (src/resident) is named
# by its own .ann: its routines and variables are @equ here, with the names that part uses.
#
# Variables outside the block: the screen, the play buffer, the resident part's routines and tables, and the work space $FE01-$FEFD
# (InitStageState $9DA1 clears $FE08-$FE5F at the stage start).
@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen's pixels
@equ $4134 EnergyBarScreen ; the HUD's energy bar: screen row 1, pixel line 1, column 20
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen's attributes
@equ $5B00 PlayBuffer 4415 ; the play buffer $5B00-$6CFF (its tail $6C3F-$6CFF is PlayBufferTail in the block): 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear; also the unpack area of StageGraphics
@equ $F959 DigitGlyphs ; resident font from '0': 8 bytes a character, 7 rows drawn (RenderDigits)
@equ $F9B0 PlaySoundVector ; resident: JP to the AY effect starter (E = the effect number)
@equ $F9BF DecimalTable 10 ; resident: the words 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1
@equ $F9CB DissolveMasks 8 ; resident: the dissolve masks; DissolveHud reads sets 0-3 (32 bytes)
@equ $F9FB Score 2 ; resident: the score's low four decimal digits, 0-9999 (AddScore)
@equ $F9FD ScoreHigh ; resident: the score's high two digits (ten thousands), 0-99 (AddScore)
@equ $FA00 BitReverse 256 ; resident: each byte with its bits reversed (the sprites drawn facing left)
@equ $FB00 ScreenLineTable 384 ; resident: the screen address of each of the 192 pixel lines (words)
@equ $FC90 KeyUp ; resident key reader: Z when UP is held (DEFINE KEYS / joystick patch its port and bit)
@equ $FC9F KeyDown ; resident key reader: Z when DOWN is held
@equ $FCAE KeyLeft ; resident key reader: Z when LEFT is held
@equ $FCBD KeyRight ; resident key reader: Z when RIGHT is held
@equ $FCCC KeyFire ; resident key reader: Z when FIRE is held
@equ $FCDB KeyHook ; resident: called before every key read (a RET, or the joystick / pause check DEFINE KEYS installs)
@equ $FE08 RandomSeed 2 ; NextSeed $8B76: seed = seed x 5 + $15 (a linear congruential step); $07CF at the stage start (InitStageState)
@equ $FE0A RandomPointer 2 ; Random $8B85: a pointer into the ROM ($0000-$3FFF), whose bytes are the random numbers; reseeded from R every 64 passes, $07CF at the stage start, $0D7A at each burst
@equ $FE0E SavedSP 2 ; ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer keep the caller's SP here while SP walks their buffers
@equ $FE10 InitOnly10 ; set to 2 by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE12 InitOnly12 ; set to 1 by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE14 WorkByte ; scratch: the placement counter of LoadRoomActors, the shape bits of StartBurst
@equ $FE17 ItemSelected ; the slot of CarriedItems the HUD cursor is on (6 at the start)
@equ $FE18 ItemLast ; the last used slot of CarriedItems (6 at the start; AddItem raises it)
@equ $FE19 ItemFirst ; the first slot of CarriedItems (6): the item window does not scroll before it
@equ $FE1C SpanCount 2 ; the spans in the span table $76A0 that CopyBuffer copies (BuildSpans $99E9)
@equ $FE1E SpanRow ; BuildSpans' cell row 0-17
@equ $FE1F CellColumn ; the cell column 2-29 of RoomChange's and BuildSpans' loops
@equ $FE21 RoomColumn ; the room's left edge in the grid, in blocks (2 cells)
@equ $FE22 RoomRow ; the room's top edge in the grid, in blocks (16 lines)
@equ $FE23 RoomGrid 2 ; the grid record of the current map grid ($9B6F, $9B8A or $9B96)
@equ $FE25 Placements 2 ; the current grid's placement list (Grid0Placements, Grid1Placements, Grid2Placements): 3 bytes a placement, $FF ends
@equ $FE27 MissileCursor ; AddMissile's round-robin slot number 0-7
@equ $FE29 CellFlag ; PutBlock $9986: the byte written to the cell's twin in $7040 (always 0)
@equ $FE2E RoomExitsPtr 2 ; the current room's byte in the grid's room table (grid record +4 + RoomNumber)
@equ $FE30 RoomNumber ; the room in its grid, a grid row of rooms after another: +1 right, -1 left, + grid record +8 down (stage 1, grid 0: 12 the demon's lair)
@equ $FE31 PassCounter ; +1 every pass (PassTick $984D): the animations' clock
@equ $FE36 EyeFlashRepeats ; DrawRoomPicture's eye flashes still to come; +1 for each object thrown into room 12's pit (CheckPitDrop $80B2)
@equ $FE37 EyeFlashStep ; DrawRoomPicture: the step 10-1 of the current flash
@equ $FE38 PitDrops ; objects thrown into room 12's pit while the demon sleeps, up to 9; the tenth object wakes it (BossPhase 2; rzx-r1: PitDrops 1 at 13880 ... 9 at 14780, BossPhase 2 at 14980)
@equ $FE39 GateOpen ; GateActor $9065: 1 while the gate stands raised (Y under $38): the left exit of its room is open
@equ $FE3A InitOnly3A ; set to $10 by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE3D BurstTimer ; the burst's step 0..$1B ($0D in the small mode); $64 idle (RoomChange sets it), $FF just started
@equ $FE3E BurstSmall ; 0 a big burst (28 steps), 1 a small one (14 steps, doubled direction steps)
@equ $FE3F Energy ; the hero's energy, 0 (empty: a life lost) to $2E (full)
@equ $FE40 InitOnly40 ; set to $0D by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE41 InitOnly41 ; set to 1 by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE42 SpanOpen ; BuildSpans: 1 while a run of open cells goes on
@equ $FE43 BossFlash ; the boss's hit flash: passes left in white-on-red ($41)
@equ $FE4A ItemsChanged ; 1 after AddItem: the main loop redraws the item strip
@equ $FE4B GridNumber ; the grid the hero is in: 0 Grid0 (stage 1: the surface and the caves), 1 Grid1 (the shaft), 2 Grid2 (the arena)
@equ $FE4C BossPhase ; the winged boss's phase: 1 asleep (the start), 2 the flight, 3 the fall (BossFlees), 4 beaten; room 12's right exit is open from 4 on
@equ $FE4D EnergyShown ; the energy the HUD bar last drew
@equ $FE4E EnergyChange ; the pending energy change: $80 and up drains 2 a pass, under $80 refills 2 a pass
@equ $FE4F SpawnDelay ; SpawnTimer $8D1D: passes to the next random spawn (a random 0-15 at the stage start)
@equ $FE50 FireLatch ; 1 while FIRE stays held after a shot or a throw: one a press
@equ $FE51 PiecesMask ; one bit a piece of the artefact (the room event's bit, actor +$10): spawned and taken
@equ $FE52 PiecesTaken ; pieces taken, 0-5
@equ $FE53 PieceFlash ; passes left of the HUD pieces' colour flash
@equ $FE54 PiecesComplete ; set to 1 when the fifth piece is taken; +1 for each item of kind 6 taken (SpawnRewardItem gives the kind-6 item while it is 1)
@equ $FE55 PieceTakenFlag ; 1 for one pass after a piece is taken
@equ $FE56 RespawnShiftX ; $FF: no death pending; else the hero's column less the respawn column less 2 (HeroDeath $B22B); the path flyers move by it (x 2) when their path ends
@equ $FE57 RespawnShiftY ; the hero's line less the respawn line less $27, set with RespawnShiftX
@equ $FE58 HeroFreeze ; passes the hero's state handler is skipped ($17 after a life lost)
@equ $FE59 LivesFlash ; the lives boxes' flash step, 0-$10 ($10 idle)
@equ $FE5A RestoreAttributes ; 1: UpdateAttributes takes the solid cells' colours from RoomAttributes once (the new room fades in over the old one)
@equ $FE5B GameOverTimer ; 0 in play; 1 when the last life is lost, counts to $32
@equ $FE5C BossHits ; the hits the winged boss's head still takes ($0A at the stage start; stays 1 after the tenth hit: BossFlees is jumped to before the store)
@equ $FE5D ArenaBossBeaten ; 1 once the arena's boss took 20 hits (ArenaBossHit): its picture and damage stop
@equ $FE5E ArenaBossHits ; the hits the arena's boss took, up to 20
@equ $FE5F ArenaFlash ; 1 after a hit on the arena's boss: its picture's colours flash red once
@equ $FE61 Lives ; lives left, from H at StageEntry
@inline $8C3D 5
@inline $8C6D 5
@inline $AA02

@module variables ; The stage's work space: the play buffer's tail, the shadow attributes, the HUD picture and the records over it
@about The block's first 5057 bytes ($6C3F-$77FF) are loaded with the stage but hold no code. $6C3F-$6CFF is the end of the play buffer PlayBuffer ($5B00-$6CFF: 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear), $6D00-$6FFF the shadow of the screen's attributes. $7000-$76BF holds, as loaded, the HUD: its picture (48 lines of 32 bytes, linear) and its colours (6 rows of 32). StageSetUp $97AC copies the colours into the shadow and dissolves the picture onto the screen (DissolveHud $8AB1); from then on the space is the stage's records: the old room's colours and the burst's particles ($7040), the room's cells ($7280), the hero's and the 13 other actors' records ($74E0, $74F2), the 16 missile records ($75E0), the digit picture ($7640) and the span table ($76A0). EndStage $789E saves the screen's HUD lines and colours back into $7000 and $7600 before the next stage's block is loaded over them.
@about An actor record (18 bytes, the hero's at $74E0 and 13 at $74F2): +0 X (byte column 0-29; $FF a free record), +1 Y (line in the play buffer), +2 width in bytes, +3 height in lines, +4/+5 the frame's bitmap, +6/+7 the handler, +8 the frame or a counter, +9 flags (bit 0 opaque, bit 4 hit, bit 7 facing left), +$0A the state, +$0B the item kind or a step, +$0C the attribute, +$0D/+$0E the base X and Y (SetActorFrame $AA02 adds the frame's dx, dy to them), +$0F flags (bit 0 shootable, bit 1 kept over a room change, bit 2 a body, bit 6 hidden, bit 7 drawn in the second pass), +$10 the placement's index or a counter, +$11 the pixel shift (1-99 drawn shifted by PreShiftSprite $7F4D).
$6C3F s PlayBufferTail ; The last 193 bytes of the play buffer PlayBuffer $5B00-$6CFF (character row 17's last lines)
> ClearBuffer $9AB5 clears the play buffer to $6CFF with PUSH HL (SP from $6D00); RoomChange $988B unpacks the stage's tiles and map into it from $5B00 (4295 bytes, to $6BC6); the actors are drawn into it every pass. Zero as loaded. Read in all four stage-1 builds (c1o, deaths, s1-idle, s1-right: CopyBuffer $9ADA).

$6D00 s ShadowAttributes ; The shadow of the screen's 768 attributes, the screen's layout; the play area from $6DC2 (row 6, column 2)
> The HUD's colours are copied into rows 0-5 at the stage's set-up (StageSetUp $97AC); RoomChange $988B writes each cell's attribute into rows 6-23, the actors' colours are painted over them every pass, and UpdateAttributes $8CAA copies the open cells to $5800 (ShowShadowAttributes $8C9D the whole of it). FillShadowAttributes $8C6D paints rectangles into it with five bytes after its CALL. Zero as loaded.
$6DC0 PlayAttributes ; row 6: the first row of the play area (the room's 18 rows)
$6DC2 PlayAttributesCell ; row 6, column 2: the room's first cell

$7000 b HudPicture 32 ; The HUD as loaded: 48 lines of 32 bytes (linear, top first), then their colours at $7600 (6 rows of 32)
> DissolveHud $8AB1 dissolves the 48 lines onto the screen's lines 0-47 and StageSetUp $97AC copies the 192 colours into the shadow rows 0-5, once, at the stage's start. EndStage $789E saves the screen's lines 0-47 back here (CopyScreenToBlock, called at $790D) and the attributes $5800-$58BF to $7600 ($78B2), so the next stage's block shows the HUD as the player left it. Between the two the bytes are the records labelled inside (RoomAttributes, Cells, HeroRecord, Actors, Missiles, DigitBuffer, SpanTable). The picture: the frame of the HUD, the energy bar's box, the score box, the item strip's box, the lives and pieces boxes (docs/img). Read in all four stage-1 builds.
$7040 RoomAttributes ; $7040-$727F: the old room's play colours (SavePlayAttrs $9FA5: 576 bytes, rows 6-23) and the cells' twins ($7042 + row x 32 + column: PutBlock writes 0, UpdateAttributes reads the solid cells' colours); also the burst's particles (StartBurst $A1F3, 4 bytes each)
$7042 RoomAttributesCell ; the twin of the cell $7282 (576 bytes lower)
$7280 Cells ; the room's cells: 19 rows of 32 (tile numbers, then their kinds after BuildSpans $99E9; bit 1 solid, bit 3 deadly, kind 7 a bridge slab)
$7282 CellsPlay ; row 0, column 2: the room's first cell (RoomCells $9928 writes 28 x 18)
$74C0 CellsFloor ; row 18 below the room: 32 bytes of $FF (StartGrid $A444), a floor no actor falls through
$74E0 HeroRecord ; the hero's actor record (18 bytes; +0 X)
$74E1 HeroY ; +1 the hero's line
$74E8 HeroFrame ; +8 the frame number of the hero's set
$74E9 HeroFlags ; +9 bit 7: facing left
$74EA HeroState ; +$0A 0 stand, 1 walk, 2 jump, 3 fall, 4 leap back, 5-7 strikes, 9 leap up, $0B recoil, $0F dying (HeroUpdate $AC3D)
$74EC HeroAttribute ; +$0C the hero's attribute
$74ED HeroBaseX ; +$0D the base column
$74EE HeroBaseY ; +$0E the base line
$74F0 HeroCounter ; +$10 the pause after a death (HeroDeath $B22B)
$74F2 Actors ; the 13 other actor records, 18 bytes each ($74F2-$75DB); +0 = $FF a free record
$75CA LastActor ; the 13th record
$75DC ActorsEnd ; 4 bytes past the records: only the HUD picture's (DissolveHud, EndStage's save) bytes
$75E0 Missiles ; the 16 missile records, 6 bytes each ($75E0-$763F): +0 the column ($FF free), +1 the line, +2 the kind (MissileHandlers $B31A), +3 to +5 the kind's own
$7600 HudColours ; the HUD's 192 colours as loaded (rows 0-5); in play the missile records 5 (its last 4 bytes) to 15 lie over them
$7610 MissilesHigh ; missile records 8-15 (AddMissileHigh $B296: the hero's death sparks)
$7640 DigitBuffer ; in play: the score's digit picture (6 + 2 columns x 8 lines, RenderScore $7B73, RevealScore $985D) and a sprite's shifted copy (PreShiftSprite $7F4D)
$76A0 SpanTable ; in play: the open spans CopyBuffer copies, 6 bytes each (the length, 0, the buffer address, the screen address; SpanCount spans), on to $779B
@res stage1/picture-hud-32x48.bin

$76C0 s SpanTableRest ; The span table's room past the HUD's colours: spans 6-42 ($76C0-$779B)
> BuildSpans $99E9 and AddSpan $9A6E write the spans from $76A0 on; a room of many short runs reaches into this space. Zero as loaded. In the stage-1 builds 34 of its bytes are read.

$779C s Unused779C ; 100 bytes no code reads or writes (the four stage-1 builds); zero as loaded


@module entry ; The stage's entry and set-up
@about Stage 1's block is entered at $7800 by the resident stage loader with H = the lives. StageEntry sets up the stage (variables, title, HUD, the first room) and falls into the main loop; EndStage returns to the loader with E = the outcome (0 game over, 1 quit, 2 stage completed), H = the lives and BC = the score's digits.
$7800 c StageEntry ; Start the stage: lives from H, variables, HUD, the first room, then the main loop
> Called by the resident stage loader with H = the lives left. Stores H in Lives, then: $9DA1 (clears $FE08-$FE5F, the carried items from StartItems, the item window at slot 6, the energy refill $2E), $97AC (the title, the HUD), $921E and $922F, RoomGrid = $9B6F (grid 0) with the actor list pointer $FE25 = $9BA0, $A4A1 and $A47D (the room's actors), RoomNumber = 2, $A444 (clears the room cells), ClearBuffer, $A5BD, $A5DF (draws the actors) and CopyBuffer, then runs on into MainLoop.
> Witness: L1 3 (rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right).

@module mainloop ; The main loop and its pass
@about MainLoop $7839 runs one game step a pass, with no frame sync: about 3 frames a pass in c1's play window, 18 at a room change (WALKTHROUGH 1.2). PacePass pads the light rooms with a busy wait. A pass ends with SPACE (the item window), CAPS SHIFT + SPACE (quit) or the end of the lives.
$7839 c MainLoop ; One pass: pace, HUD, input, actors, draw, copy; SPACE opens the item window
> The pass, in order: PacePass, ShowPieceTaken, FlashPieces, CheckPause (ENTER), $8D1D, RedrawItemsIfChanged, ClearBuffer, CheckStageExit (may leave to EndStage), the missiles $B2E6, $A5BD, $A5DF (the actors drawn into the buffer), $89BB, $8A2E, $8930, $A28B, KeyHook, $8CAA (attributes and CopyBuffer), $984D (energy, lives flash, game over step), ShowScore, then the SPACE test $8A54.
> SPACE with CAPS SHIFT ends the stage with E = 1 (QuitStage); SPACE alone opens ItemWindow unless the hero is in state $0F (dying; the hero record's +$0A at $74EA). The loop goes on while Lives is not 0 or the hero's state is not 0; with no lives and the hero back in state 0 it ends with E = 0 (GameOverExit).
> Witness: L1 19500 (c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right).
$7877 MainLoopSpace ; SPACE pressed: CAPS SHIFT too quits, else the item window
$7889 MainLoopNext ; go on while lives are left or the hero is not back in state 0
$7897 c GameOverExit ; No lives: end the stage with E = 0
> Reached from MainLoop when Lives and the hero's state $74EA are both 0. E = 0, then EndStage.
> Witness: L1 1 (s1-right).
$789C c QuitStage ; CAPS SHIFT + SPACE: end the stage with E = 1
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right); known only from the
> code. $787E, the JP Z to it, ran 3 times in c1 (SPACE seen, CAPS SHIFT not).
$789E c EndStage ; Leave the stage: hide the HUD boxes, save the HUD, fade, return E, H = lives, BC = the score's digits
> E (pushed) is the outcome: 0 game over (GameOverExit), 1 quit (QuitStage), 2 stage completed (StageExit). Clears the play buffer, hides the pieces boxes and the lives boxes with two inline attribute fills ($8C3D), saves the HUD attributes (rows 0-5) to $7600, clears the score, the two middle HUD fields, the item strip and the pieces field with CopyToScreen from the cleared buffer (stride 0), saves the HUD bitmap (lines 0-47) to $7000 ($8A89), fades the screen (FlashFadeScreen), clears it ($8B92), waits 100 frames ($8C35) and returns to the stage loader with E, BC = ScoreDigitsHigh (the six score digits) and H = Lives.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r1, s1-right).
$78A5 b EndPiecesBox 5 ; $8C3D's inline record: column 25, line 24, 6 x 2 cells, attribute 1 (the pieces boxes hidden)
$78AA c EndStageLives ; EndStage, continued: hide the lives boxes
> Part of EndStage, after the first inline record.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r1, s1-right).
$78AD b EndLivesBox 5 ; $8C3D's inline record: column 1, line 24, 6 x 2 cells, attribute 1 (the lives boxes hidden)
$78B2 c EndStageSave ; EndStage, continued: save the HUD, clear its fields, fade, return
> Part of EndStage, after the second inline record.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r1, s1-right).

@module render ; The renderer: the sprite row plotters, the play buffer, the attributes, ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer
@about A pass draws the actors into the play buffer $5B00-$6CFF (18 character rows of 8 pixel lines of 32 bytes, linear: a pixel line is +32, a character row +256) with the row plotters below, then copies to the screen only the open cells of the room (the spans BuildSpans made at the room change), so the scenery drawn once by RoomChange stays in front of the actors. The attributes go the same way: the shadow $6D00 (768 bytes, one a screen cell) to the screen for the open cells only.
$7925 c FlashFadeScreen ; Fade every coloured ink up to white over 7 frames, then down to black over 7 frames
> Seven times (HALT each): every attribute whose ink is neither 0 nor 7 gets ink + 1. Then seven times (two HALTs each): every ink not 0 gets ink - 1. Inputs: none; changes the whole attribute area $5800-$5AFF. Called by EndStage.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r1, s1-right).
$7927 FadeUpFrame
$792F FadeUpCell
$7939 FadeUpNext
$7944 FadeDownFrame
$794D FadeDownCell
$7953 FadeDownNext

@module mainloop
$795D c PacePass ; Reseed the random pointer every 64 passes and pad the pass with a busy wait in the light rooms
> When PassCounter & $3F is 0, the high byte of RandomPointer is set from R. Then: in grid 0 (GridNumber 0), rooms 0-5 wait $044C rounds of DelayBC; in grid 1, room 0 waits $0640 (PaceShaftRoom); every other room goes on at once. The wait evens out the pass time of rooms with few actors (8978 of the 10187 passes in the stage-1 recordings waited).
> Witness: L1 19500 (c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right).
$796F PacePassRoom
$7982 c PacePassUnused ; A pacing variant no code calls: rooms 0 and 5 wait $03E8, room $0B waits a count left in BC
> No caller in the image (no CALL, JP or pointer to $7982). Reads RoomNumber: 0 or 5 wait $03E8 rounds of DelayBC, $0B waits BC as it stands (the LD HL,$16A8 before it sets HL, not BC), others return. A leftover of another stage's pacing.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right); known only from the code.
$7996 PacePassUnusedWait
$799C c PaceShaftRoom ; Grid 1, room 0: wait $0640 rounds
> Reached from PacePass when GridNumber is not 0: in grid 1 room 0 waits $0640 rounds of DelayBC, else returns.
> Witness: L1 731 (rzx-r1).

@module util ; Small helpers: keys, clears, copies, numbers, random numbers, delays
@about Clears and copies of the screen and the shadow, the decimal printing helpers, the random numbers (Random $8B85 reads ROM bytes through RandomPointer; NextSeed $8B76 an LCG), WaitFrames and the small arithmetic the others share.
$79AB c DelayBC ; Busy wait: count BC down to 0
> Input BC (the rounds, 26 T-states each). Output BC = 0, A = 0. The interrupt returns land on its three instructions (L1 lists them as entries).
> Witness: L1 12491743 (c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right).
$79AC DelayBCTest
$79AE DelayBCLoop

@module mainloop
$79B1 c CheckPause ; ENTER pauses: wait for its release, a second press and its release
> Reads port $BFFE bit 0 (ENTER). Not pressed: returns at once. Pressed: waits for the key's release, the next press and its release, so the game stands still between two presses. No other effect.
> Witness: L1 19502 (c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right).
$79B9 PauseRelease
$79BF PausePress
$79C5 PauseRelease2

@module render
$79CC c CopyToScreen ; Copy a block of bytes to the screen, line by line
> Inputs: HL = the source, B = the screen column, C = the first pixel line, D = the width in bytes, E = the lines, A = the source's stride (added to HL after each line; 0 repeats one source line, used with the cleared buffer to clear a screen block). Patches the column into $79E5 and the stride into $79F6, then for each line takes the line's address from ScreenLineTable and LDIRs D bytes. Destroys IX, BC, DE.
> Witness: L1 20920 (c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right).
$79DF CopyToScreenLine

@module hud ; The energy, the lives, the score, the HUD, game over and the stage exit
@about The score is six decimal digits in two resident variables, ScoreHigh (two digits) and Score (four digits, 0-9999), so it carries from stage to stage. The energy (Energy, 0-$2E) changes by 2 a pass towards a pending EnergyChange; the HUD's six boxes at the top left show the lives, and the five boxes at the top right the pieces taken.
$79FC c CheckStageExit ; With item 6 selected, standing at the start place of room 2: leave the stage
> Every pass. Only in grid 0 (GridNumber 0), room 2 (the stage's first room) and with item 6 selected (GetSelectedItem): when the hero's x ($74E0) is 18-21 and its y ($74E1) is $5A, drops its own return address and runs StageExit. In stage 1 the selected item 6 at that place is the way out of the stage.
> Witness: L1 19501 (c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right).
$7A1D c StageExit ; The stage's exit effect: falling stars over a coloured field until FIRE or SPACE, then EndStage with E = 2
> StartStageExit draws the field and seeds 80 stars at $5B00 (4 bytes each); then each frame (HALT) moves the stars of speed 1-3 (MoveStar), until KeyFire or SPACE ($8A54); then E = 2 and EndStage. rzx-r1: after frame 29744 (the stars from about 29800).
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r1).
$7A21 StageExitFrame
$7A28 StageExitStar
$7A45 StageExitDone
$7A4A c MoveStar ; Move one star down by its speed and plot it as two pixel lines
> IX = the star: +0 speed 1-4, +1 the pixel within the byte 0-3, +2 the column 2-29, +3 y ($80 and up: not yet on screen). Off screen: y += speed only. On screen: y = (y + speed) mod 128, clears the bytes above it (speed lines, from ScreenLineTable+96, line 48 down), and plots two lines from StarPixels (speed and pixel).
> Witness: L1 38454 (rzx-r1).
$7A58 MoveStarOnScreen
$7A61 MoveStarPlot
$7A8A MoveStarClear
$7ABA b StarPixels 8 ; The two pixel lines of a star, by speed (rows 1-4) and pixel (pairs 0-3)
@res stage1/table-star-pixels.bin
$7ADA c StartStageExit ; Clear the play area, colour it at random and seed 80 stars
> $A057, then clears the play area (column 0, lines $30-$BF, 32 bytes wide, from the blank $8BA3 with stride 0), RandomPlayAttrs, and 80 star records at $5B00: speed 1-4, pixel 0-3, column 2-29, y $80-$FF (random bytes from $8B85).
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r1).
$7AF4 SeedStar
$7B06 SeedStarColumn
$7B27 c RandomPlayAttrs ; Fill the play area's attributes (28 x 16 cells) with bright inks 2-7 on black
> From $58C2 (row 6, column 2), 16 rows of 28 cells: bright, ink 2-7 from $8B85, paper 0. Sets RandomPointer to $091D first, so the colours are the same each time.
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r1).
$7B33 RandomPlayAttrsRow
$7B36 RandomPlayAttrsCell
$7B37 RandomPlayAttrsPick
$7B53 c AddScore ; Add BC points to the score
