@module hero ; The hero: walk, jump, crouch, strike, fire, the items and the item window
@about The carried items are two 12-byte lists, CarriedItems $7F17 (the item kind of each slot) and CarriedCounts $7F23 (its amount), filled from StartItems at the stage's start. Slots 0-5 are padding (slots 0-3 hold the blank icon 4) and slot 6 is the first item; ItemFirst..ItemLast are the slots in use and ItemSelected the selected one. The HUD's item strip shows the selected slot in the middle and its neighbours (DrawItemStrip, 8 icons drawn, 3 and two halves seen through the 12-byte window at $406A); the SPACE item window (ItemWindow) scrolls it.
$7C27 c ItemWindow ; SPACE: stop the game, flash the strip's frame, choose an item with LEFT and RIGHT, SPACE again to go on
> Clears PassCounter, waits (cycling the frame colours, CycleWindowFrame) for SPACE's release, then every 6 frames: DrawItemStrip and ShowItemCount; RIGHT scrolls to the previous slot (ScrollItemsRight), LEFT to the next (ScrollItemsLeft); SPACE again: waits for its release, cycles the frame back to its first colour and flashes the selected box (FlashSelectedBox).
> Witness: L1 245 (rzx-r1).
$7C35 ItemWindowStep
$7C37 ItemWindowFrame
$7C4F ItemWindowLeft
$7C59 ItemWindowSpace
$7C5E ItemWindowRelease
$7C63 ItemWindowSettle
$7C6E c FlashSelectedBox ; Colour the selected item's box with inks 2 to 6, one a frame
> Five frames: patches the colour into the inline record SelectedBoxRecord (column 15, line 24, 2 x 2 cells) and fills it with $8C3D. Called by ItemWindow and at the stage's start ($981B).
