@module missiles ; The missiles: shots, thrown objects and flyers in 16 six-byte records at $75E0
@about $B2E6 calls, for each of the 16 records at $75E0 not free (+0 = $FF), the handler of its kind (+2) from the table at $B31A. The record: +0 the column (path flyers: +5 / 2), +1 y, +2 the kind, +3/+4/+5 the kind's own (a step, a direction). A handler frees its record with $B35E. Most of them draw with $B42B / $B446 (normal / mirrored) and colour with $B382, $B3A3 or $B40A / $B46F.
$8006 c UpdateThrownArc ; Kinds 2 and 3: an object thrown in an arc, left (2) or right (3); counts the drops into room 12's pit
> IY = the record: +3 the arc step, +4 the frame counter. CheckPitDrop first; below y $82 it is freed. +3 and +4 step; CheckArcLanding at steps 12 and 21; step 22 frees it. Every fourth tick x moves 1 (kind 2 left, 3 right); y += ArcSteps[+3]. Draws frame +4 & 7 from $D926 (12 bytes a frame) with the record ArcFrame, mirrored for kind 3.
> Witness: L1 170 (rzx-r1).
$8013 ThrownArcMove
$8037 ThrownArcLeft
$803A ThrownArcDraw
$8071 ThrownArcMirror
$8079 b ArcSteps 8 ; The arc's y change at each step 0-22
