@module actors ; The actor records: placement, the per-pass update, the frames, the bursts
@about The 14 actor records at $74E0 (the hero, then 13 others at $74F2), 18 bytes each: +0 X (column 0-29, $FF a free record), +1 Y (line in the 144-line play buffer; $C8 and up is above the top), +2 width in bytes, +3 height in lines, +4/+5 the frame's address, +6/+7 the handler, +8..+$0C the kind's five bytes (+9 bit 0 opaque, bit 7 facing left; +$0C the attribute), +$0D/+$0E X and Y where the actor entered the room, +$0F flags (bit 0 shootable (ShotHitsActor), bit 1 kept over a room change, bit 2 a body (IsColumnTaken), bit 6 not drawn, bit 7 drawn in the second pass), +$10 the placement's index, +$11 the pixel shift (0 or 100 and up: none).
$8B37 c StepFineRight ; Move the actor IY right by A eighths of a byte column (no caller)
> Adds A to the fraction +$11; past 8 takes 8 off and moves +0 and +$0D one column right. Nothing calls it (no
> CALL, JP or table word names $8B37): a leftover of the engine.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: c1o, deaths, rzx-r1, s1-idle, s1-right); known only from the code.
