@module rooms
$9B6F b Grid0 9 ; Grid 0's record (stage 1: the surface and the caves): 69 x 21 blocks, the start window at block column 22, row 0, the room table Grid0Rooms, map offset 0, 6 rooms a grid row
> A grid record, 9 bytes: +0 the width and +1 the height in blocks, +2/+3 the start window's block column and row (where StartGrid $A444 puts the window; the grid passages rewrite them, $ABBA-$AC30), +4/+5 the room table, +6/+7 the grid's offset in the map section of the unpacked graphics, +8 the rooms a grid row of rooms. A room is a window of 14 x 9 blocks; the windows step 11 block columns and 6 block rows, so neighbouring rooms share 3 columns or 3 rows of blocks. RoomGrid ($FE23) points at the record of the hero's grid; RoomCells $9928 reads +0, +6/+7; RoomNumber counts the windows a grid row after another.
> The room table, one byte a room: the exits, bit 0 right, bit 1 left, bit 2 up, bit 3 down (read by the edge checks $AADA). Item kind 7 writes 5 into room 12's byte $9B84 (right and up: the gate to the right opens).
> Read in all four stage-1 builds (RoomCells, StartGrid, the edge checks). The file rooms.txt holds the three records, their room tables and the placement lists; tools/fig_rooms.py draws the map and every room from it (docs/img/maps/).
$9B78 Grid0Rooms ; 18 rooms, 6 a row: the exits of each
$9B8A Grid1 ; Grid 1 (stage 1: the shaft): 14 x 21 blocks, start 0, 0, map offset $05A9, 1 room a row (3 rooms)
$9B93 Grid1Rooms
$9B96 Grid2 ; Grid 2 (stage 1: the dragon's arena): 14 x 9 blocks, one room, map offset $06CF
$9B9F Grid2Rooms
$9BA0 Grid0Placements ; grid 0's 66 placements: the kind (bit 7: done), X and Y in cells over the whole grid; $FF $FF $FF ends
> LoadRoomActors $A4CC puts each placement not done that lies in the room's window (X in 2 x RoomColumn to + 29, Y in 2 x RoomRow to + 17) into a free actor record, with the kind's row of ActorKinds; MarkPlacementDone sets bit 7 when the actor is beaten or taken, so it does not come back; ResetObjectLists $922F clears the bits at the stage's start. Grid 0: kinds 0 and 1 (hanging bodies) 7 each, 2 (flame jets) 15, 3-6 (urns and chests) 16, 7 (fire pits) 13, 8-11 (the winged demon's parts) 1 each, 12 and 14 (statue heads) 1 each, 13 (the gate) 1, 16 (the bridge slab) 1.
$9C69 Grid1Placements ; grid 1's 4: statue heads (kinds 12, 14)
$9C78 Grid2Placements ; grid 2's 5: four fire pits and the dragon's head (kind 15)
@res stage1/rooms.bin

@module actors
$9C8A b ActorKinds 9 ; The 17 placement kinds, 9 bytes each: the Y offset, the handler, 5 bytes for the record's +8 to +$0C, the record's +$0F
> LoadRoomActors $A4CC builds an actor from a placement with its kind's row: +1 Y = the placement's Y x 8 + the offset, +6/+7 the handler, +8 to +$0C (the counter, the flags, the state, the item, the attribute), +$0F (bit 0 shootable: ShotHitsActor; bit 1 kept over a room change: LoadRoomActors). Stage 1's kinds: 0 and 1 a hanging body (HangingActor $9186; 1 faces the other way), 2 a flame jet (FlameJetActor $8DCC), 3-6 urns and chests that break when struck (StrikeableActor $A7C4; +$0B the item inside), 7 a fire pit (FirePitActor $8D6D), 8-11 the winged demon's left wing, right wing, body and head (BossWingLeft $8E60 to BossHead $8E86), 12 and 14 a statue head (StatueActor $912B), 13 the gate (GateActor $9065), 15 the dragon's head (ArenaHeadActor $90E7), 16 the bridge slab (BridgeSlabActor $90A3). Read in all four stage-1 builds (81 of its bytes: the kinds of the rooms the recordings visit).
@res stage1/table-kinds.bin

$9D23 b ActorTemplates 18 ; Seven whole actor records (18 bytes each, the first the bridge slab's) that SpawnActor $A4B1 copies for the actors no placement makes
